    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1050"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Wright to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    translations of the ordinances relating to the government-general of Kwantung,
                    together with some editorial comments<anchor n="a" xml:id="d171-f1"/> of the
                    Japanese press. These ordinances are to go into effect on September 1.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Luke E. Wright.</hi></signed></closer>











